(Week 2 lecture: convex sets and convex functions) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A set is convex when the straight segment between any two of its) Tj T*
(points stays inside the set. Balls, half-spaces, and polyhedra are) Tj T*
(convex. A crescent shape is not.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A function f is convex when its epigraph is a convex set.) Tj T*
(Equivalently, for every x, y and every t between 0 and 1:) Tj T*
(f\(t x + \(1 - t\) y\) <= t f\(x\) + \(1 - t\) f\(y\).) Tj T*
ET
